TEXT -112 144 Left 2 !.tran 0 5s 0 0.1ms
TEXT -112 152 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}\n.options vntol=100m abstol=1m reltol=0.003
TEXT 272 200 Left 2 ;General:\n \nThis model is a synchronous generator without transformer and regulation of voltage and speed\nThe speed is regulated externally\nThe voltage is regulated externally\n \n \n \nparams:\n            UN_verkettet=20000 Nominal voltage\n            IN=14.434k Nominal current\n            Pel=400e6 Nominal power (UN_verkettet*IN*cosphi of 0.8)\n            Kc=0.5 short-circuit ratio (0.4-0.5 cylindrical pole, 0.8-1.0 salient pole)\n            UE0=600V Nominal field voltage\n            IE0=2000A Nominal field current\n            p=2 Number of poles      \n            Schenkelpolfactor=0.5 for salient pole machine (kc=0.8-1.0)\n                                              1 for cylindrical pole machine(kc=0.4-0.5)    \n             Daempferfaktor=1 (damping factor)\n             Streuung=0.05 (leakage factor)\n             rcu=0.01 (rel. Copper resistance)\n             rbg=0.001 (rel. friction moment)\n             J=100000 (inertia)\n             n0=1500 starting speed\n             err0=0 (best do not change this)\n             a=0.9 parameter for nonlinear saturation\n             m=7 parameter for nonlinear saturation\n \nAlternative Elemente: (wechsle mit Doppelklick auf SpiceModel-Zeile                   \n                  keine   \n          \nHINT: The power output can be computed with M*314.159/2  (P=M*omega/p)\n                    The load angle can be outputed with V(u1:u1:theta) \n                    The here constant frequency is n/30    2*n/60 = p*n/60 (p=Polcount)\n \nLibfile: Sgen.lib
TEXT 64 256 Left 2 !.param RN=0.4 LN={40/314.159}
TEXT -416 344 Left 2 !Verr0 verr 0 pwl 0s 1800v 0.7s 600v
TEXT -8 136 Left 2 ;Reltol set to 0.005, vntol to 100m !!\nsince simulation otherwise to slow
TEXT -136 496 Left 2 ;The voltage regulation is with a external PWL source\nThe AVR is not constructed because there is\nno need of it
TEXT -424 352 Left 2 ;(Min=200v Max=1800v 600v=nominal)
TEXT -136 424 Left 2 ;The speed controller is on at the beginning\nAt 1s the block is synchronized  \nAt 2s there is a load step of 100MW
TEXT -72 368 Left 2 ;After 2s there is a load step \nof 100MW which is sourced\nby the voltage source and \nby the generator
TEXT -144 352 Left 2 !.param PN=100e6 QN=0
TEXT -320 472 Left 2 ;> nominal torque
TEXT -240 472 Left 2 ;friction torque
TEXT -400 488 Left 2 ;Since the frequency of the network is here\nexactly 50Hz there is no need to switch \noff the speed regulator of the generator\nAt normal condition the regulator has to be\nswitched off after synchronizing the machine\nYou can test it by a example with two\nsynchronous machine one bigger for the\nnet and one smaller for synchronizing it to\nthe first one
TEXT -416 136 Left 4 ;Generator at a network \nwith voltage source
TEXT 144 352 Left 2 ;Dphi=180 degrees\nfor optimal synchronizing\nconditions
TEXT -304 304 Left 2 ;More exciting voltage at the beginning \nfor faster startup to nominal voltage
